{
    "_comment": [
        "CANONICAL RSC cross-layer contract fixture. Consumed by:",
        "  PHP  tests/Unit/Rsc/RscContractTest.php (reactive-1 app suite)",
        "  Rust readyset-util/src/reverb_http.rs #[cfg(test)] (vendored copy at readyset-businesspress/fixtures/)",
        "  JS   packages/businesspress/core/resources/js/rsc/auth-hash.test.mjs (node --test)",
        "Identity formula (authoritative: RscGraphQLCache::getAuthContext + core-channels.php rsc.{authHash}):",
        "  authHash = md5(user_id . \":\" . (shop_id ?? \"none\") . \":\" . scope), scope defaults to \"customer\"; anonymous = literal \"anon\".",
        "twin_identities: canonical (cache_name, param_key) -> rs:hyd twin key encoding.",
        "  Producers: PHP RscTwinIdentity::paramKey/twinKey (pdeps registration + TwinStore)",
        "             Rust DfValue Display join('|') (reader.rs extract_key_column_values +",
        "             eviction_key_values) + redis_notifier.rs twin_key().",
        "  param_key = per-binding canonical strings joined with '|' in PLACEHOLDER order.",
        "  Value encoding is DfValue-Display-canonical: NULL->\"NULL\", false->\"0\", true->\"1\",",
        "  numbers -> decimal string, strings verbatim (NO escaping: a literal '|' in a value",
        "  is structurally ambiguous but both sides join identically so keys still match;",
        "  a lone value \"_\" collides with the empty-params form; timestamp params may",
        "  mismatch the engine's TimestampTz Display - all documented, accepted).",
        "  Empty params -> param_key \"\" -> twin key rs:hyd:{cache_name}:_",
        "invalidation_events: wire shape of the Reverb `rsc.invalidated` event emitted by the Rust bridge.",
        "  data is the DOUBLE-ENCODED (Pusher protocol) JSON string; fields serialize in ALPHABETICAL order",
        "  (serde_json without preserve_order): {\"epoch\":N,\"keys\":[...]}. epoch = post-INCR value of the",
        "  per-channel counter rs:epoch:{authHash} (literal `anon` suffix for the shared channel), INCRed",
        "  once per channel per delivered batch and visible in Redis BEFORE the event is broadcast.",
        "  epoch null = the INCR failed; the event then ships WITHOUT the field (legacy shape) - consumers",
        "  MUST treat a missing epoch as uncomparable, never as 0.",
        "Regenerate ONLY via the generator script and re-vendor the Rust copy (check-rsc-contract-sync.sh)."
    ],
